<td id="S3.T1.2.21.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;"></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.21.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;"></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.21.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;"></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.21.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.21.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:142.3pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.21.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">- Self-evaluation of confidence in generated answers</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T1.2.22" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.2.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;"></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;"></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.22.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;"></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.22.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.22.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:142.3pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.2.22.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">- Optimizing reasoning pathways for efficiency and accuracy</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ III-C Model Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ Dynamic Reasoning Chains through Depth-Specialized Mixture-of-Experts in Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a> summarises the different expert types used in the proposed architecture, detailing their reasoning depth, core specialisation, and representative tasks. The experts range from shallow pattern recognisers to deep logical reasoners and supervisory meta-cognitive modules, highlighting the hierarchical and adaptive nature of the system
Each expert <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t+1}=E_{j}(h_{t};\theta_{j})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t+1}=E_{j}(h_{t};\theta_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> Eq.<a href="#S3.E1" title="In III-C Model Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ Dynamic Reasoning Chains through Depth-Specialized Mixture-of-Experts in Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is the hidden state at time <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are the expert parameters specialized to reasoning depth <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Routing Network:</span>The <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> serves as the core innovation of the architecture, responsible for dynamically selecting the appropriate experts to process a given input <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. This mechanism enables adaptive reasoning depth, allowing the system to allocate computational resources efficiently according to the complexity of the input<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>.
Input Complexity Estimation: To determine which experts to activate, the routing network first estimates the complexity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> of the input using multiple indicators:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Syntactic complexity</span>: Measured as the depth of the parse tree, <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{syn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{syn}</annotation></semantics></math>, capturing the structural intricacy of the sentence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Semantic density</span>: Represented by the number of unique concepts per sentence, <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{sem}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{sem}</annotation></semantics></math>, reflecting the richness of information embedded in the input.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reasoning steps required</span>: Estimated via clause chaining or logical decomposition, <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating the minimum number of reasoning operations necessary to reach a solution.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">These indicators are combined into a single <span id="S3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">complexity score</span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(X)=\alpha d_{syn}+\beta c_{sem}+\gamma r" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(X)=\alpha d_{syn}+\beta c_{sem}+\gamma r</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta,\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta,\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq.<a href="#S3.E2" title="In III-C Model Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ Dynamic Reasoning Chains through Depth-Specialized Mixture-of-Experts in Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> are learned parameters that weight the relative importance of each factor. This score guides adaptive depth selection and expert activation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Expert Selection: The routing probability for each expert <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed as:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(E_{j}\mid X)=\text{softmax}(W\cdot\phi(X))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(E_{j}\mid X)=\text{softmax}(W\cdot\phi(X))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(X)</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq.<a href="#S3.E3" title="In III-C Model Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ Dynamic Reasoning Chains through Depth-Specialized Mixture-of-Experts in Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> denotes the feature representation of the input, capturing both syntactic and semantic information, and <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> are trainable routing parameters. By applying a softmax over all experts, the network generates a probability distribution that reflects the relevance of each expert for the current input. This methodology presents a hierarchical expert routing architecture (see Fig. <a href="#S3.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ III-C Model Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ Dynamic Reasoning Chains through Depth-Specialized Mixture-of-Experts in Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> that dynamically selects and composes specialized processing modules based on input complexity. The system employs a routing network <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> using softmax-based probability distributions <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(E_{j}|X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(E_{j}|X)</annotation></semantics></math> to select top-<math id="S3.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> experts from three depth levels: shallow experts (SPE1-3) for basic pattern recognition and knowledge retrieval, medium-depth experts (CRE1-3) for multi-step inference and contextual integration, and deep experts (LIE1-3) for abstract reasoning and theorem proving. A complexity estimation mechanism computes a composite score <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(X)=\alpha\cdot d_{syn}+\beta\cdot c_{sem}+\gamma\cdot r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(X)=\alpha\cdot d_{syn}+\beta\cdot c_{sem}+\gamma\cdot r</annotation></semantics></math> to guide dynamic chain composition <math id="S3.SS3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(E_{i_{1}})(h_{0}),E_{i_{2}}(\cdot),\ldots,E_{i_{n}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(E_{i_{1}})(h_{0}),E_{i_{2}}(\cdot),\ldots,E_{i_{n}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, while the training framework optimizes a joint loss function combining task performance (<math id="S3.SS3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{task}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{task}</annotation></semantics></math>), routing accuracy (<math id="S3.SS3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{routing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{routing}</annotation></semantics></math>), and load balancing (<math id="S3.SS3.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{balance}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{balance}</annotation></semantics></math>) to ensure efficient resource utilization and high performance across variable computational requirements.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">To improve efficiency and reduce unnecessary computation, experts are activated <span id="S3.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">sparsely</span>, using a top-<math id="S3.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selection strategy:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(X)=\{E_{j}\mid P(E_{j}\mid X)\text{ is in top-}k\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is in top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(X)=\{E_{j}\mid P(E_{j}\mid X)\text{ is in top-}k\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p">This ensures that only the most relevant experts contribute to the reasoning process for a given input, promoting both computational efficiency and focused inference.
Dynamic Chain Composition: Once the experts are selected, the reasoning chain is dynamically constructed to propagate information through multiple levels of depth. The output hidden state <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{out}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{out}=C(E_{i_{1}}(h_{0}),E_{i_{2}}(\cdot),\dots,E_{i_{k}}(\cdot))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{out}=C(E_{i_{1}}(h_{0}),E_{i_{2}}(\cdot),\dots,E_{i_{k}}(\cdot))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i_{1}},\dots,E_{i_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i_{1}},\dots,E_{i_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq.<a href="#S3.E5" title="In III-C Model Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ Dynamic Reasoning Chains through Depth-Specialized Mixture-of-Experts in Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> denote the activated experts. This composition allows coherent information flow across different reasoning depths, effectively capturing multi-step dependencies and maintaining context-aware processing<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>.
Overall, the routing network enables <span id="S3.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">adaptive, depth-aware reasoning</span>, combining sparse expert selection with dynamic chain construction to efficiently handle inputs of varying complexity while preserving reasoning quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training and Optimisation:</span>The training procedure is designed to progressively stabilise expert specialisation and routing behaviour, ensuring both the individual experts and the overall reasoning architecture converge effectively. The training is structured into a staged curriculum:
Expert Pre-training
Each expert module <math id="S3.SS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{E_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{E_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> is initially trained on datasets aligned with its specialisation:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span>Expert Types and Their Pre-training Datasets</figcaption>
<table id="S3.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expert Type</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:335.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-training Dataset</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Shallow Pattern Experts (SPE)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:335.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Factual QA datasets for pattern recognition and knowledge retrieval</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Compositional Reasoning Experts (CRE)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:335.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Logic puzzles, arithmetic, and multi-step inference problems</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Logical Inference Experts (LIE)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:335.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Legal and abstract reasoning texts to improve formal logic and proofs</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Memory Integration Experts (MIE)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:335.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Long-context stories for narrative comprehension and context tracking</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Meta-Cognitive Experts (MCE)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:335.7pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Synthetic tasks requiring adaptive strategy control and dynamic depth adjustment</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ III-C Model Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ Dynamic Reasoning Chains through Depth-Specialized Mixture-of-Experts in Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a> summarises the different types of experts employed in the architecture along with their corresponding pre-training datasets. Each expert type is specialised for specific reasoning or pattern recognition tasks, ranging from shallow factual retrieval to deep logical inference and adaptive meta-cognitive strategies, ensuring comprehensive coverage across diverse problem domains.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Routing Network Integration:</span> The routing network <math id="S3.SS3.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is trained to dynamically select relevant experts based on input complexity. Training begins with simple examples and gradually introduces more complex inputs, allowing the network to learn to allocate reasoning depth effectively without destabilising pre-trained experts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-Expert Chain Training:</span> As routing decisions become reliable, multi-expert chains are trained to process complex tasks<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>. The hidden representations from activated experts are composed sequentially to generate the final reasoning output:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\text{out}}=C\big(E_{i_{1}}(h_{0}),E_{i_{2}}(\cdot),\dots,E_{i_{k}}(\cdot)\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\text{out}}=C\big(E_{i_{1}}(h_{0}),E_{i_{2}}(\cdot),\dots,E_{i_{k}}(\cdot)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p20.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i_{1}},\dots,E_{i_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i_{1}},\dots,E_{i_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq.<a href="#S3.E6" title="In III-C Model Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ Dynamic Reasoning Chains through Depth-Specialized Mixture-of-Experts in Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> are the activated experts and <math id="S3.SS3.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the chain composition function.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">End-to-End Joint Optimisation :</span> The system is trained end-to-end using a combined loss function that balances task accuracy, routing fidelity, and expert utilisation:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=L_{\text{task}}+\lambda_{1}L_{\text{routing}}+\lambda_{2}L_{\text{balance}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>task</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>routing</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>balance</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=L_{\text{task}}+\lambda_{1}L_{\text{routing}}+\lambda_{2}L_{\text{balance}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p21.2" class="ltx_p">In Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="In III-C Model Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ Dynamic Reasoning Chains through Depth-Specialized Mixture-of-Experts in Transformer Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>:</p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{task}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>task</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{task}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cross-entropy loss for task predictions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{routing}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>routing</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{routing}}</annotation></semantics></math> measures routing accuracy against annotated ground truth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{balance}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>balance</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{balance}}</annotation></semantics></math> imposes a load-balancing penalty to prevent expert collapse and encourage uniform utilisation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.SS3.p21.3" class="ltx_p">This joint optimisation ensures both accurate task performance and efficient, balanced expert usage.
<span id="S3.SS3.p21.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theoretical Efficiency Analysis:</span> For a uniform transformer with depth <math id="S3.SS3.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and sequence length <math id="S3.SS3.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\text{uniform}}=O(dn)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>uniform</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\text{uniform}}=O(dn)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p21.4" class="ltx_p">For the DS-MoE architecture with sparse expert activation <math id="S3.SS3.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS3.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\ll d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\ll d</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\text{DS-MoE}}=O(k\log n)+O(n)_{\text{routing}}\approx O(k\log n)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>DS-MoE</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>routing</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\text{DS-MoE}}=O(k\log n)+O(n)_{\text{routing}}\approx O(k\log n)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p21.5" class="ltx_p">This represents a significant reduction in computation while maintaining reasoning quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Memory Complexity:</span> Memory usage is similarly reduced:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\text{uniform}}=O(dn),\quad O_{\text{DS-MoE}}=O(kn)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>uniform</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>DS-MoE</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\text{uniform}}=O(dn),\quad O_{\text{DS-MoE}}=O(kn)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p22.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p22.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expected Gains:</span> For typical transformer configurations (<math id="S3.SS3.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=24</annotation></semantics></math>) and sparse expert activation (<math id="S3.SS3.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[2,5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[2,5]</annotation></semantics></math>), the DS-MoE framework achieves approximately 70–80% computational savings, with negligible routing overhead relative to the reduction in depth.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE III: </span>Comparison of Complexity between Uniform Transformer and DS-MoE</figcaption>
<table id="S3.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T3.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:2pt;padding-bottom:2pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:28.5pt;">
